                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\tfrac{\mathrm{i}}{\hbar}S\big(\mathbf{\Phi})\big)
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:EquationSchwingerDyson"} (1)
            may be understood as the result of path-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integration+by+parts"}> integration by parts
            , whereby the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variational+calculus"}> variational
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
            of the observable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on the right is moved over to the factor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
